00:00:53,100 --> 00:01:02,740
CONVERSATION 1
We are down to two candidates for one position, and we need to decide by the end of the day in order to finalize this whole procedure.

2
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:05,740
Yes, but it isn’t an easy choice to make.

3
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:08,620
Both applicants are quite strong.

4
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:09,980
Let’s get to it then.

5
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:15,240
Both of them went to good universities, and both of them studied business-related subjects.

6
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:18,980
So, academically, I’d say they’re pretty much the same.

7
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:19,600
What do you think?

8
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,020
I would agree.

9
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:21,560
Yes.

10
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:29,700
The only difference worth noting, perhaps, is that it looks like Rachel scored moderately stronger grades throughout high school and university.

11
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:33,360
But as I said, only a tiny bit higher than Peter.

12
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:35,020
That’s true and worth noting.

13
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:35,960
Thank you.

14
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:38,680
In addition, Rachel interviewed very well.

15
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,600
I thought she came across as bright and alert.

16
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:42,540
Yes.

17
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:48,140
She asked some very good questions about the position and the company, which made me think she is very keen about the job.

18
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,100
I thought so too.

19
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,020
Now let’s look at Peter’s interview performance.

20
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,060
I thought he also did very well.

21
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:58,280
He came across as respectful and professional.

22
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,480
Wouldn’t you say?

23
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:02,820
Calm and poised; very mature for his age.

24
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:03,800
Exactly.

25
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:08,520
In my notes, I wrote that he seemed composed and in control of his emotions.

26
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,840
I think he definitely looked more mature than Rachel.

27
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,720
Interesting.

28
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:24,300
So we agree that Rachel appeared inexperienced and less mature than Peter, even though both candidates are the same age and have practically no work experience.

29
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:29,400
When comparing them side by side, yes, Peter seemed more self-assured, somehow.

30
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,940
Maybe it was something about their body language.

31
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:32,620
Sure.

32
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:35,040
Maybe he was simply less nervous.

33
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,920
Maybe.

34
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:36,880
Who knows?

35
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,260
To be honest, I think I like Rachel better.

36
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,240
Hmm, really?

37
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,880
I think I like Peter.

38
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:57,420
Ah, well, if there’s a tie and we can’t come to an agreement, then we’ll take it to John and let him cast the deciding vote.

